{
  "version": "0.6.0",
  "notes": "Harden the cellular path (new cellular.py, shared by ota.py and sheets_log.py, replacing two duplicated copies of the same thin AT-command sequence). Every 'cellular data did not open' failure so far skipped straight to AT+NETOPEN with no check the modem was even responding, no SIM check, and no wait for network registration -- NETOPEN commonly fails if the modem hasn't attached to the tower yet, which can take up to a minute. Sim7600Modem now checks AT liveness, AT+CPIN? (SIM ready), waits for CREG/CGREG/CEREG registration with CSQ signal logged throughout, retries NETOPEN once after NETCLOSE if it errors, and raises a SPECIFIC reason (not responding / no SIM / not registered / NETOPEN failed / IPADDR failed) instead of one generic message. New cellular_test.py: bare cellular connectivity test, no Sheets/Apps Script setup needed. sheets_log_test.py now forces prefer_wifi=False so it actually exercises the cellular path being tested.",
